Student Performance Analytics System
Python Mini Project Documentation
This project analyzes a 20-student marks dataset and produces individual grades, class and subject summaries, a top-five ranking, and pass/fail counts. The supplied output reports an overall class average of 69.03 and 16 PASS / 4 FAIL results.
Student and submission details
Field	Details
Student name	[Enter student name]
Roll number	[Enter roll number]
Class / department	[Enter class or department]
Institution	[Enter institution name]
GitHub repository URL	[Add GitHub repository URL]

1. Objective
Build a Python program that reads student marks and attendance, calculates totals and averages, assigns grades and pass/fail outcomes, and presents useful class-level insights in a readable terminal report.
2. Technologies used
Technology	Use
Python 3.10 or later	Program logic and calculations
pandas	CSV loading, tabular calculations, sorting, and summaries
CSV	Portable student records input

3. Dataset description
The sample contains 20 student records. The dataset columns are Student_ID, Name, Department, Python, Maths, English, and Attendance. Subject marks are out of 100. Totals and averages in the report are calculated from Python, Maths, and English. The expected input filename is student_performance.csv, subject to the filename used in the source code.
4. Implementation
1.	Load the CSV dataset into a pandas DataFrame.
2.	Calculate each student's total and average across the three subjects.
3.	Apply the grade bands and the PASS/FAIL threshold.
4.	Compute the class average, minimum and maximum averages, subject averages, top five, and pass/fail counts.
5.	Print the student-wise summary and complete report.
Grade and result rules
Grade	Average
A+	90 and above
A	80 to below 90
B	70 to below 80
C	60 to below 70
D	50 to below 60
F	Below 50

The output treats an average below 50 as FAIL. Dev's average is 48.67, so the accurate row is grade F, result FAIL. With this correction, the summary is 16 PASS and 4 FAIL.
5. Key features
•	Student-wise total and average marks
•	Letter grade and pass/fail classification
•	Class highest, lowest, and overall averages
•	Subject-wise averages
•	Top-five student ranking
•	Pass/fail statistics and complete student report
