8. Final outcome
The program converts the sample dataset into a concise performance report. It identifies the class average as 69.03, reports subject averages of 68.30 in Python, 68.95 in Maths, and 69.85 in English, and shows 16 students passing and 4 failing.
9. Challenges and learning
The project practices loading structured data, selecting numeric columns, computing derived values, sorting by performance, and applying consistent grade rules. Cross-checking each student's result against the class totals is essential: Dev's 48.67 average belongs in the F / FAIL category, producing the required 16 PASS and 4 FAIL totals.
10. Setup and run
6.	Install Python 3.10 or later.
7.	Create and activate a virtual environment: python -m venv .venv (Windows: .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1; macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate).
8.	Install pandas: python -m pip install pandas.
9.	Place student_performance.csv beside the Python script.
10.	Run the program: python student_performance.py (replace with the actual source filename).
